sual-timeline.html#body-03" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Diverse Innovations and Evolving Trends</div></a></section></section><header id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd54b-d511608f" class="break"><div data-w-id="a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd54c" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="header-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c7d4bace5a342dfc11a2c8_center-focused-ivy-growth-ui-page-break-animation.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></header></address><article id="body-01" class="section body-part"><h3 class="h3">Emergence of a Design Style</h3><div class="body-portion"><h4 id="w-node-ecda73c2-4ab9-e7d5-5079-5d39469ed78f-d511608f" class="h4-2">Industrial Design: The Dawn of Functionality</h4><div class="paragraph-list w-richtext"><h2>What’s a Rich Text element?</h2><p>The rich text element allows you to create and format headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, images, and video all in one place instead of having to add and format them individually. Just double-click and easily create content.</p><h4>Static and dynamic content editing</h4><p>A rich text element can be used with static or dynamic content. For static content, just drop it into any page and begin editing. For dynamic content, add a rich text field to any collection and then connect a rich text element to that field in the settings panel. Voila!</p><h4>How to customize formatting for each rich text</h4><p>Headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, figures, images, and figure captions can all be styled after a class is added to the rich text element using the &quot;When inside of&quot; nested selector system.</p></div></div><div class="art-history"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f3ab1e1cf999fb30da882b/64db8d1a2546910c930be35b_full.henry-dreyfuss-model-phonograph-wood-metal-camden-usa-1925.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Henry Dreyfuss, &quot;Model A Phonograph&quot;, Wood and metal, Camden, USA, 1925." class="period-artwork"/><div class="image-attribution">Henry Dreyfuss, &quot;Model A Phonograph&quot;, Wood and metal, Camden, USA, 1925.</div></div><section class="break"><div class="header-animated-ui" data-w-id="ecda73c2-4ab9-e7d5-5079-5d39469ed7a0" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c7d75deb70a956cf7fad2b_end-focused-ivy-growth-animation-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></section></article><article id="body-02" class="section body-part"><h3 class="h3">Peak of an Art Movement</h3><div class="body-portion"><h4 id="w-node-_4319c37e-edca-9369-758b-17d674e840e5-d511608f" class="h4-2">The Zenith of User-Centered Design</h4><div class="paragraph-list w-richtext"><h2>What’s a Rich Text element?</h2><p>The rich text element allows you to create and format headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, images, and video all in one place instead of having to add and format them individually. Just double-click and easily create content.</p><h4>Static and dynamic content editing</h4><p>A rich text element can be used with static or dynamic content. For static content, just drop it into any page and begin editing. For dynamic content, add a rich text field to any collection and then connect a rich text element to that field in the settings panel. Voila!</p><h4>How to customize formatting for each rich text</h4><p>Headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, figures, images, and figure captions can all be styled after a class is added to the rich text element using the &quot;When inside of&quot; nested selector system.</p></div></div><div class="art-history"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f3ab1e1cf999fb30da882b/64db8d1a2546910c930be360_full.eliot-noyes-selectric-typewriter-plastic-metal-new-york-usa-1961.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Eliot Noyes, &quot;Selectric Typewriter&quot;, Plastic and metal, New York, USA, 1961." class="period-artwork"/><div class="image-attribution">Eliot Noyes, &quot;Selectric Typewriter&quot;, Plastic and metal, New York, USA, 1961.</div></div><section class="break"><div class="header-animated-ui" data-w-id="4319c37e-edca-9369-758b-17d674e840e8" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c7d75deb70a956cf7fad2b_end-focused-ivy-growth-animation-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></section></article><article id="body-03" class="section body-part"><h3 class="h3">Evolution of an Art Legacy</h3><div class="body-portion"><h4 id="w-node-_6d07a57a-b6ec-073f-4813-47e66254f2ed-d511608f" class="h4-2">Diverse Innovations and Evolving Trends</h4><div class="paragraph-list w-richtext"><h2>What’s a Rich Text element?</h2><p>The rich text element allows you to create and format headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, images, and video all in one place instead of having to add and format them individually. Just double-click and easily create content.</p><h4>Static and dynamic content editing</h4><p>A rich text element can be used with static or dynamic content. For static content, just drop it into any page and begin editing. For dynamic content, add a rich text field to any collection and then connect a rich text element to that field in the settings panel. Voila!</p><h4>How to customize formatting for each rich text</h4><p>Headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, figures, images, and figure captions can all be styled after a class is added to the rich text element using the &quot;When inside of&quot; nested selector system.</p></div></div><div class="art-history"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f3ab1e1cf999fb30da882b/64db8d1a2546910c930be363_full.apple-design-team-apple-macintosh-portable-plastic-electronics-cupertino-usa-1989.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Apple Design Te