icon" data-w-id="94e12e08-f8a6-45ce-64bf-9fc39ec3a3d3" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c9434d8a60ceb743414e7a_rainbow-arch-menu-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></nav></header></div><address style="opacity:0" class="header-section"><header id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd503-d511608f" class="path"><a href="../../index.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Home</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="../../the-style-spectrum.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Style Spectrum</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html" aria-current="page" class="url w-inline-block w--current"><div class="path-page">Minimalism</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html#timeline" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Visual Timeline</div></a></header><header id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd516-d511608f" class="title-block"><h1 class="title w-dyn-bind-empty"></h1></header><section class="summary-block"><section class="callout"><div class="teaser"></div><h2 id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd525-d511608f" class="h2">Minimalism Started Stark Before Subtle</h2><p class="paragraph-700">Minimalism was stark when it was born; it’s decline led to a much more nuanced finale. The redefinition of simplicity in art.</p></section><section class="in-page-links"><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html#body-01" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">The Essence of Minimalism</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html#body-02" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Minimalism&#x27;s Bold Statement</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html#body-03" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Diversifying Simplicity</div></a></section></section><header id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd54b-d511608f" class="break"><div data-w-id="a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd54c" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="header-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c7d4bace5a342dfc11a2c8_center-focused-ivy-growth-ui-page-break-animation.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></header></address><article id="body-01" class="section body-part"><h3 class="h3">Emergence of a Design Style</h3><div class="body-portion"><h4 id="w-node-ecda73c2-4ab9-e7d5-5079-5d39469ed78f-d511608f" class="h4-2">The Essence of Minimalism</h4><div class="paragraph-list w-richtext"><h2>What’s a Rich Text element?</h2><p>The rich text element allows you to create and format headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, images, and video all in one place instead of having to add and format them individually. Just double-click and easily create content.</p><h4>Static and dynamic content editing</h4><p>A rich text element can be used with static or dynamic content. For static content, just drop it into any page and begin editing. For dynamic content, add a rich text field to any collection and then connect a rich text element to that field in the settings panel. Voila!</p><h4>How to customize formatting for each rich text</h4><p>Headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, figures, images, and figure captions can all be styled after a class is added to the rich text element using the &quot;When inside of&quot; nested selector system.</p></div></div><div class="art-history"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f3ab1e1cf999fb30da882b/64db8d2759fa7d8ee2046e94_full.tony-smith-die-steel-new-york-1960.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Tony Smith, &quot;Die&quot;, Steel, New York, 1960." class="period-artwork"/><div class="image-attribution">Tony Smith, &quot;Die&quot;, Steel, New York, 1960.</div></div><section class="break"><div class="header-animated-ui" data-w-id="ecda73c2-4ab9-e7d5-5079-5d39469ed7a0" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c7d75deb70a956cf7fad2b_end-focused-ivy-growth-animation-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></section></article><article id="body-02" class="section body-part"><h3 class="h3">Peak of an Art Movement</h3><div class="body-portion"><h4 id="w-node-_4319c37e-edca-9369-758b-17d674e840e5-d511608f" class="h4-2">Minimalism&#x27;s Bold Statement</h4><div class="paragraph-list w-richtext"><h2>What’s a Rich Text element?</h2><p>The rich text element allows you to create and format headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, images, and video all in one place instead of having to add and format them individually. Just double-click and easily create content.</p><h4>Static and dynamic content editing</h4><p>A rich text element can be used with static or dynamic content. For static content, just drop it into any page and begin editing. For dynamic content, add a rich text field to any collection and then connect a rich text element to that field in the settings panel. Voila!</p><h4>How to customize formatting for each rich text</h4><p>Headings, paragraphs, blockquotes, figures, images, and figure captions can all be styled after a class is added to the rich text element using the &quot;When inside of&quot; nested selector system.</p></div></div><div class="art-history"><img src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63f3ab1e1cf999fb30da882b/64db8d2859fa7d8ee2046e98_full.donald-judd-untitled-stack-galvanized-iron-new-york-1967.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Donald Judd, &quot;Untitled (Stack)&quot;, Galvanized iron, New York, 1967." class="period-artwork"/><div class="image-attribution">Donald Judd, &quot;Untitled (Stack)&quot;, Galvanized iron, New York, 1967.</div></di