ist"><div class="w-dyn-empty"><div>No items found.</div></div></div><div class="w-dyn-list"><div class="w-dyn-empty"><div>No items found.</div></div></div></div></div><section class="boarder-ui"><div class="divider" data-w-id="a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd673" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c9eb594fc24b0a1d62b26b_geometric-ground-plant-animation.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="2" data-duration="0"></div></section></section><section style="opacity:0" class="sources"><h3 id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd675-d511608f" class="h3">Sources</h3><div class="source"><a href="https://www.widewalls.ch/artists/agnes-martin" target="_blank" class="source-hyperlinked-page-title w-inline-block"><h4 class="source-website">Agnes Martin / Agnes Bernice Martin</h4></a><p id="w-node-_379e95df-2652-9a31-4fa4-afd5baeb2f50-d511608f">Most recognized for her evocative paintings marked out with pale color washes and subtle pencil lines, Agnes Martin was a Canadian-born American artist, whose conviction of the emotive and expressive power of art shaped her career. She sought inspiration in the spiritual realm rather than the intellect and strongly …</p></div><div class="source"><a href="https://www.artsy.net/artwork/agnes-martin-untitled-number-1-1" target="_blank" class="source-hyperlinked-page-title w-inline-block"><h4 class="source-website">Collection: Fondation Louis Vuitton, Paris</h4></a><p>Agnes Martin’s intricate, fine-lined grids, bands, and blocks of muted color convey the artist’s lifelong search for serenity and sublime beauty. The late painter drew her singular style from influences that ranged from Abstract Expressionism and Minimalism to Zen Buddhism and American …</p></div><div class="source"><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2015/may/22/agnes-martin-the-artist-mystic-who-disappeared-into-the-desert" target="_blank" class="source-hyperlinked-page-title w-inline-block"><h4 class="source-website">Agnes Martin: the artist mystic who disappeared into the desert</h4></a><p>When she returned to painting in 1971, the grids had gone, replaced by horizontal or vertical lines, the old palette of grey and white and brown giving way to glowing stripes and bands of very pale pink and blue and yellow. “Sippy cup colours”, the critic Terry Castle once called them, and their titles likewise …</p></div></section><footer style="opacity:0" class="footer"><aside class="form-block"><div id="1602-spectrum-footer-timeline-email" class="standard-form-block w-form"><form id="wf-form-" name="wf-form-" data-name="#1602-spectrum-footer-timeline-email" method="get" class="footer-form" data-wf-page-id="64f5584e81052e45d511608f" data-wf-element-id="a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd68e"><input class="form-field w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd68f-d511608f w-input" maxlength="256" name="1602-name" data-name="1602-name" placeholder="Name" type="text" id="1602-name" required=""/><input class="form-field w-input" maxlength="256" name="1602-email" data-name="1602-email" placeholder="Email" type="email" id="1602-email" required=""/><input type="submit" data-wait="Trending..." id="w-node-a73bbd67-1541-8c9c-fd0e-5ef2bcfcd691-d511608f" class="subscribe-maroon w-button" value="Subscribe"/></form><div class="subscription-thanks w-form-done"><div class="message">Thanks, rockstar 💎</div></div><div class="subscription-error w-form-fail"><div class="message">Hm — try that again please? </div></div></div></aside><div class="logo-contact-block"><div class="footer-menu-block"><a href="minimalism-visual-timeline.html#" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="footer-text">About</div></a><a href="../../about/contact.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="footer-text">Contact</div></a><div class="legal"><a href="../../about/legal-privacy-terms.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class=