ion="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></nav></header></div><address style="opacity:0" class="header-section"><header class="path"><a href="../index.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Home</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="../the-style-spectrum.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">The Style Spectrum</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="brutalism.html" aria-current="page" class="url w-inline-block w--current"><div class="path-page">Brutalism</div></a></header><header id="w-node-_59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a40160-d511601d" class="art-divider"><div class="header-ui" data-w-id="59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a40161" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64f456557a05afc618fb6cb9_brutalism-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div><h1 class="h1 hidden">Brutalism</h1></header><header id="w-node-_59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a40164-d511601d" class="title-block"><div id="w-node-_59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a40165-d511601d" class="title-subtitle-group design-style"><h2 class="title">Powerful Architectural Statement</h2><div class="subtitle">Common for government buildings and institutional settings.</div></div><section class="in-page-links"><a href="brutalism.html#introduction-art-history-brutalism" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Brief Intro</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="brutalism.html#brutalism-art-history-articles" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Article Series</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="brutalism.html#brutalism-artist-interpretation" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Concept Art</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="brutalism.html#" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">More Styles</div></a></section></header></address><div id="w-node-_59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a4017e-d511601d" style="opacity:0" class="section"><div class="column peacock-anim"><div data-w-id="59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a40180" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64daf55bb56ed775d9564a27_peacock-fan.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div></div></div><section style="opacity:0" class="section"><header id="introduction-art-history-brutalism" class="header-subtext-group design-style"><h3 class="design-style-header">Not-so-subtle Power Statements</h3><div class="subtext">Perfect for propaganda!</div></header><article class="_2-column"><div class="column design-style-subheader"><h4 class="design-style-subheader">Philosophy</h4></div><div class="column design-feature-body"><p class="paragraph">Brutalism looks to make statements of power and leave a lasting visual impact. That&#x27;s why it is so common for governmental buildings. <br/></p><p class="paragraph">It emerged in the mid-20th century. <br/></p></div></article><article class="_2-column"><div class="column design-style-subheader"><h4 class="design-style-subheader">Characteristics</h4></div><div class="column design-feature-body"><div class="paragraph">Brutalism most commonly by the bold use of concrete — something we&#x27;ve learned a hard lesson from as our cities and urban centers bake in the climate change caused excessive heat. <br/></div><div class="paragraph">The style is characterized by imposing, fortress-like structures, emphasizing raw materials and functionality.<br/></div></div></article></section><section id="astro-fashion" style="opacity:0" class="cta"><div data-w-id="59ed257b-a581-1438-f5f1-862d54a4019d" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="cta-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.