" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></nav></header></div><address style="opacity:0" class="header-section"><header class="path"><a href="../index.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Home</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="../the-style-spectrum.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">The Style Spectrum</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="mid-century-modern.html" aria-current="page" class="url w-inline-block w--current"><div class="path-page">Mid-Century Modern</div></a></header><header id="w-node-_1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0adc-d51160d1" class="art-divider"><div class="header-ui" data-w-id="1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0add" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64f45656233beaba8191104a_mid-century-modern-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div><h1 class="h1 hidden">Mid-Century Modern</h1></header><header id="w-node-_1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0ae0-d51160d1" class="title-block"><div id="w-node-_1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0ae1-d51160d1" class="title-subtitle-group design-style"><h2 class="title">Retro That Never Left</h2><div class="subtitle">Sleek, iconic vintage style.</div></div><section class="in-page-links"><a href="mid-century-modern.html#mid-century-modern-art-history-intro" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Brief Intro</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="mid-century-modern.html#mid-century-modern-art-history-articles" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Article Series</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="mid-century-modern.html#mid-century-modern-artist-interpretation-concept-art" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Concept Art</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="mid-century-modern.html#" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">More Styles</div></a></section></header></address><div id="w-node-_1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0afa-d51160d1" style="opacity:0" class="section"><div class="column peacock-anim"><div data-w-id="1335b709-ceb0-82bf-bd01-94f0c6cc0afc" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64daf55bb56ed775d9564a27_peacock-fan.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div></div></div><section style="opacity:0" class="section"><header id="mid-century-modern-art-history-intro" class="header-subtext-group design-style"><h3 class="design-style-header">Made For The Organic Feel</h3><div class="subtext">Iconic pieces are shaped with precision</div></header><article class="_2-column"><div class="column design-style-subheader"><h4 class="design-style-subheader">Philosophy</h4></div><div class="column design-feature-body"><p class="paragraph">Sleek almost isn&#x27;t enough of a descriptor for Mid-Century Modern perfectionism. It is as if the goal was to make a formless-form: a chair that appears as if it grew naturally that way. <br/></p><p class="paragraph">It should be of no surprise that Mid-Century Modern design places an emphasis on functionality with a connection to nature. It often features large windows and open spaces. <br/></p></div></article><article class="_2-column"><div class="column design-style-subheader"><h4 class="design-style-subheader">Characteristics</h4></div><div class="column design-feature-body"><div class="paragraph">This retro style is characterized by its soft curves, organic forms, and iconic vintage pieces. It emerged in the mid-20th century and remains influential today. <br/></div></div></article></section><section id="astro-fashion" style="opacity:0" class="cta"><div data-w-id="1335b709