a6-45ce-64bf-9fc39ec3a3d3" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c9434d8a60ceb743414e7a_rainbow-arch-menu-ui.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0"></div></nav></header></div><header id="w-node-_3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf4235f-d511610c" class="section full-width-header-anim"><div class="header-ui" data-w-id="3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf42360" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64daebf91d2af4475d9e372f_ornate-calligraphic-page-heading.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="1" data-is-ix2-target="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="2" data-duration="0"></div></header><div class="section page-path"><header class="path"><a href="index.html" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="path-page">Home</div></a><div class="path-page">  /  </div><a href="the-style-spectrum.html" aria-current="page" class="url w-inline-block w--current"><div class="path-page">The Style Spectrum</div></a></header></div><main style="opacity:0" class="header-section"><header id="w-node-_3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf4232a-d511610c" class="title-block"><div id="w-node-d86a1286-69f2-a3d3-d4c5-3295148fc7b9-d511610c" class="title-subtitle-group center"><h1 class="title">The Style Spectrum</h1><div class="subtitle">Modern take on historic storytelling</div></div><section class="in-page-links"><a href="the-style-spectrum.html#why-art-history" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Why Art History</div></a><div class="in-page-link">   •    </div><a href="the-style-spectrum.html#relevant-art-history-styles" class="url w-inline-block"><div class="in-page-link">Design Style Sections</div></a></section><div class="column header-summary"><div class="paragraph header-summary">Style is a language of personality. Art&#x27;s history sheds light onto the patterns in designs evolution over time, from art movement to art movement. Knowledge that empowers us to understand, predict, and influence design. Stories that provide us with the foundation needed for the creative jobs of tomorrow. </div></div><div id="w-node-_6ea58dd7-fdff-11d6-a379-ff2c2f27c634-d511610c" class="page-break"><div class="column-40 _20"><div class="row-flex"><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="59cc3f97-5170-4999-32f0-7bc1d4c76eb4" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="6ea58dd7-fdff-11d6-a379-ff2c2f27c635" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="e43ffca6-8fe7-6c49-e972-ab4a91d8d74d" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div></div></div></div></header></main><section id="why-art-history" style="opacity:0" class="section"><header class="header-subtext-group center"><h2 class="h2">Looking Back Through Art</h2><div class="subtext">Historic Art Movements</div></header><article class="section-article"><h3 class="h3 left">Evolutionary Pathways</h3><div class="paragraph _800">Look for elements of The Style Spectrum&#x27;s featured art you recognize blended into design around you today, in home decor magazines, or the wall of your favorite local coffee shop. <br/></div><div class="paragraph _800">Historic work constantly re-inspires contemporary design. It layers, forever finding new ways to tell the same visual stories. <br/></div><div class="paragraph _800">Pay attention to the art that preceded a movement and what it turned into. Similar to modern graphic design across the web or fresh styles that fashion adopts, they all evolve as the months and seasons pass. <br/></div><h3 class="h3 left">Observing Patterns</h3><div class="paragraph _80 center">» Strengthen our own foundation for creative work <br/>» Better understand others by how they visually express themselves <br/>» Develop personal style <br/>» Anticipate the non-stop evolution and design&#x27;s next move </div></article></section><section style="opacity:0" class="section"><div class="page-break"><div class="column-40 _20"><div class="row-flex"><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="0665bacc-81d3-66a8-7514-7ce9d1fb59a7" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="0665bacc-81d3-66a8-7514-7ce9d1fb59a8" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div><div data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-w-id="0665bacc-81d3-66a8-7514-7ce9d1fb59a9" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64dae6a8ca772baa81f62fbd_calligraphic-spiral-diamond.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div></div></div></div><header id="relevant-art-history-styles" class="header-subtitle"><h2 class="h2">Design Style Spectrum</h2><div class="subtext centered"> 12 Art Movements Relevant Today</div></header><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/sustainable-eco-friendly.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Sustainable Eco-friendly Design</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Withstanding Climate Change Fury</h4><div class="paragraph-700">At our current pivotal juncture, design is beginning to reflect the reality of our surroundings.</div><div class="paragraph-700">Modern life&#x27;s awareness has given rise to a recognizable design ethos—one that embraces style while representing our response to mitigate climate disasters. </div><div class="paragraph-700">Uncover how it intertwines aesthetics with a sustainable, resilient vision of the future. </div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/biophilic-design-coexist-nature.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Biophilic Design</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Echoing the Harmony of Nature</h4><div class="paragraph-700">A compelling trend of artful infusion of interiors with the natural world. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Its essence lies in creating spaces that encourage us to remember how much we love nature; that we want to coexist. This is a hopeful effort at connecting society to the profound consequences that seem to be otherwise diminished by being in the news daily. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Explore the visual aspects and underlying principles.<br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/industrial-design-renewed-popularity.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Industrial Design</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Form Follows Function</h4><div class="paragraph-700">This concept emerged as a defining principle in design spanning 1920s to 1940s, championing utilitarian simplicity in every detail. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Initially thriving during its era, this style has surged in modern popularity. Look towards the sleek lines of tech or the minimalist elegance of furniture. Or find it in popular restaurants. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Dig into why the design philosophy has found new relevance. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/postmodernism.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Post-modernism</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Seeking Innovation</h4><div class="paragraph-700">An embrace of the unconventional and unexpected from 1970s to 1990s. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Beyond its historical significance, it has an unconventional spirit that prompts us to question traditional paradigms and explore — perhaps shaping sustainable design approaches of tomorrow. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">It lives on today through trendsetters aspiring towards leaving distinctive marks on today&#x27;s design landscape. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/brutalism.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Brutalism</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Unapologetically Concrete</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Easily defined by its composition material and bold character, spawned in 1950s to 1970s. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Its impact on contemporary architectural undeniable as its reminder of Urban Heat Islands (is it surprising climate change is becoming part of most every conversation?). In a rather aggressive way it is nudging us towards finding more livable approaches to architecture and design and reevaluate past choices. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Learning about its legacy prompts us to look towards a resilient future. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/scandinavian-design.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Scandinavian Design</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Poignant Principles</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Clean lines and functional beauty flourished in the 1950s and 1960s. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Most evident today in contemporary interiors where simplicity meets elegance. Another timeless guide for trend spotters. It relevance extends beyond aesthetics, pointing towards what functional design means today. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">You&#x27;ll see how its principles shape spaces in a way that echos the changing mentality of society towards weather. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/bauhaus.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Bauhaus</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Interdisciplinary Collaboration</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Grounding art and function&#x27;s marriage in 1919 to 1933. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Born as a collaborative effort to bridge the gap between traditional art and industrial design, the movement brought together artists, craftsmen, and designers. This effort left an indelible mark on design. It built the foundation for today&#x27;s era of versatile artistry, inspiring our current innovative creative landscape — like combining Art History and Astrology! <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Dig into their focus on integration of creativity and utility through innovation. <br/></div></div></article></section><section id="astro-fashion" style="opacity:0" class="cta"><div data-w-id="470d80cf-e549-8906-5e3a-5a729bc640ca" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="cta-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64daf55b19c92a97ddd08337_left-peacock-fan.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="2" data-duration="0"></div><div class="cta-form"><h3 id="w-node-_470d80cf-e549-8906-5e3a-5a729bc640cc-d511610c" class="h3 cta">New Article Notifications</h3><div class="cta-message">Subscribe for a heads up when a new article series is published. Check the the outline on their feature pages for what&#x27;s to come. <br/></div><div id="102-home-section-email" class="standard-form-block w-node-_470d80cf-e549-8906-5e3a-5a729bc640d1-d511610c w-form"><form id="wf-form-1501-spectrum-updates-email" name="wf-form-1501-spectrum-updates-email" data-name="1501-spectrum-updates-email" method="get" class="spectrum-updates-email" data-wf-page-id="64f5584e81052e45d511610c" data-wf-element-id="470d80cf-e549-8906-5e3a-5a729bc640d2"><input class="form-field w-input" maxlength="256" name="1501-name" data-name="1501-name" placeholder="Name" type="text" id="1501-name" required=""/><input class="form-field w-input" maxlength="256" name="1501-email" data-name="1501-email" placeholder="Email" type="email" id="1501-email" required=""/><input type="submit" data-wait="Thanks! " class="subscribe-light-purple w-button" value="Subscribe"/></form><div class="subscription-thanks w-form-done"><div class="message">Check your inbox 🪐</div></div><div class="subscription-error w-form-fail"><div class="message">Weird. Try that again, please? </div></div></div></div><div data-w-id="470d80cf-e549-8906-5e3a-5a729bc640dc" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="cta-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64daf55bbf49c009ffdc57bc_right-peacock-fan.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="2" data-duration="0"></div></section><section style="opacity:0" class="section"><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/art-deco-evolving-maximalism-geometry.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Art Deco</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Geometric Opulence</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Defined by opulence and geometric elegance, the design era of the 1920s and 1930s remains an everlasting source of trendsetting inspiration. </div><div class="paragraph-700">Today, as our obsession with Maximalism marks a shift from minimalism, it&#x27;s fascinating to recognize how the formless evolves into the geometric, often drawing inspiration from the historic Art Deco movement. This enduring style has influenced the ever-evolving landscape of design more than once. </div><div class="paragraph-700">Get insight into where today&#x27;s love for Maximalism is headed next. </div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/mid-century-modern.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Mid-Century Modern</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Timeless Sophistication</h4><div class="paragraph-700">This design era of the 1940s to the 1960s has long served as a touchstone for today&#x27;s design trailblazers. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Recognize it from our current virtual obsession, and note how trends tend to exhaust themselves before shifting. This is another style that offers a glimpse into where our collective design taste is headed next. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Discover how Mid-Century Modern maintains this enduring allure. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/maximalism.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Maximalism</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Organized Chaos</h4><div class="paragraph-700">It&#x27;s not difficult to spot Maximalism everywhere in the contemporary design landscape. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Defined by eclectic chaos and vibrant excess, this daring and often intricate style can be a challenge to master. It is so &quot;now&quot; — this recent resurgence offers valuable insight into aesthetic evolution. From the structure reminiscent of Art Deco to the spatial and contextual shifts akin to Pop Art and even the mesmerizing world of Vaporwave. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Note how the louder design trends quickly rise and shift, and how Maximalism is both a reflection and a catalyst of our ever-changing design sensibilities. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/minimalism-departing-legacy.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Minimalism</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Tranquil Simplicity</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Key to understanding and setting trends across the decades. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Notably, it stands out amidst the rather abrupt move away from minimalism into the vibrant world of Maximalism. However, even as design preferences shift, Minimalism leaves an mark on our collective aesthetic consciousness. Its enduring legacy is, in part, due to our craving both simplicity and extravagance. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">It lives on today through trendsetters aspiring towards leaving distinctive marks on today&#x27;s design landscape. <br/></div></div></article><article class="row-side-header left"><div class="column-30"><a href="learn-design-trends/pop-art-transformative-return.html" class="content-link w-inline-block"><h3 class="h3 left">Pop-Art</h3></a></div><div class="column-70"><h4 class="h4 gold">Doja Cat Is Andy Warhol</h4><div class="paragraph-700">Emerging in the 1950s and 1960s, Pop-Art&#x27;s influence transcends its origins. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Defined by vibrant colors and bold patterns, its legacy continues to inspire modern visionaries, such as musical and visual artist Doja Cat, often considered our contemporary equivalent to the iconic Andy Warhol. <br/></div><div class="paragraph-700">Explore the dynamic and colorful movement, and the imagination of those who dare to push boundaries and challenge convention.<br/></div></div></article></section><div style="opacity:0" class="separator"><div data-w-id="a026efda-fbec-57d1-724a-e348a506d842" data-is-ix2-target="1" class="animated-ui" data-animation-type="lottie" data-src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/63eeb040bbd9e6ee6a1ef49e/64c9eb594fc24b0a1d62b26b_geometric-ground-plant-animation.lottie" data-loop="0" data-direction="1" data-autoplay="0" data-renderer="svg" data-default-duration="2" data-duration="0" data-ix2-initial-state="0"></div></div><footer style="opacity:0" class="footer"><aside class="form-block"><div class="standard-form-block w-form"><form id="wf-form-1502-spectrum-footer-email" name="wf-form-1502-spectrum-footer-email" data-name="1502-spectrum-footer-email" method="get" class="footer-form" data-wf-page-id="64f5584e81052e45d511610c" data-wf-element-id="3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf42474"><input class="form-field w-node-_3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf42475-d511610c w-input" maxlength="256" name="1502-name" data-name="1502-name" placeholder="Name" type="text" id="1502-name" required=""/><input class="form-field w-input" maxlength="256" name="1502-email" data-name="1502-email" placeholder="Email" type="email" id="1502-email" required=""/><input type="submit" data-wait="Trending..." id="w-node-_3fde19c5-f26c-ab62-f653-7385adf42477-d511610c" class="subscribe-mint-green w-button" value="Subscribe"/></form><div class="subscription-thanks w-form-done"><div class="message">Thanks, rockstar 💎</div></div><div class="subscription-error w-form-fail"><div class="message">Hm — try that again please? <